Thomas Mayer wrote:
> Moonsilence wrote:
> 
>>What is the difference between "writing in the dust" (this is done with
>>fingers?) and "engraving"?
> 
> Engraving is slower, but lasts longer, so it is semi-permanent.

It depends. Engraving with an athame or a wand of digging requires
just _a single turn_, while engraving with a hard gem, or - which is
usually not recommended - with a weapon requires one turn per letter.

> Permanent messages can be burned into the floor with some special objects.

Burning into the floor is a one-turn move as is scribbling in the
dust with some marker, or writing with your fingers.

